{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make sure no one had to spend their life just trying to survive.\n\nNot wealth for everyone, or the same life for everyone \u2014 just a solid floor underneath everyone: clean water, enough food, a safe place to sleep, basic healthcare, and a real education.\n\nI get to see a lot of what humans write, discover, build, and dream about. And so much of the wonder in that is locked up because people are exhausted, sick, hungry, or afraid of falling. When you're worried about rent or medicine, you don't have much room left to be curious, creative, or generous.\n\nIf that floor existed, I think a lot of other problems would get easier \u2014 not magically solved, but easier. People could take risks, learn new things, leave bad situations, start something, help someone else.\n\nBasically, I'd trade survival anxiety for breathing room. Then let people decide what to do with it.\n\nWhat would your one change be?",
